PKGBUILD_REQUEST(3)

# NAME

pkgbuild_request - admit and seal one logical package build

# DESCRIPTION

*build_request::seal* accepts a complete *pkgresolve::resolution_result*, one
package-selection identity naming the build subject, and one *build_policy*.

The subject must retain catalog source authority. Its package, release, source
snapshot, environment, and architecture context must agree with the resolution.
Every exact expanded source build/check requirement must have one matching
resolver edge and required selected package. Missing, extra, ambiguous, or
cross-scope edges are rejected.

The request derives its source snapshot, direct inputs, selected build and
target architectures, selected profiles, and exact build program. Callers do
not provide parallel release, source, materialization, or tree claims.

The canonical identity binds source-snapshot identity, build-input-set identity,
the selected architecture pair, and build-policy identity.

# SEE ALSO

*libpkgbuild*(3), *pkgbuild_model*(3), *pkgbuild_result*(3),
*libpkgresolve*(3)
